# csdd sandbox — egress allow-list.
# One host per line; blank lines and #-comments are ignored. init-firewall.sh
# resolves each host to its current IPv4 addresses and permits ONLY those.
# Keep this list minimal: every entry widens what a bypass-mode session can reach.

# --- Anthropic / Claude Code ---
api.anthropic.com
statsig.anthropic.com
sentry.io

# --- GitHub ---
github.com
api.github.com
codeload.github.com
objects.githubusercontent.com
ghcr.io

# --- npm (Claude Code runtime + tooling) ---
registry.npmjs.org

# --- VS Code / devcontainers ---
update.code.visualstudio.com
marketplace.visualstudio.com

# --- Ubuntu apt ---
archive.ubuntu.com
security.ubuntu.com
ports.ubuntu.com

# --- Language registry presets ---
# `csdd sandbox init --feature <name>` un-comments the matching registries below
# (or add hosts with --allow-domain). Left commented, they stay blocked.
# [go]     proxy.golang.org sum.golang.org
# [python] pypi.org files.pythonhosted.org
# [rust]   static.crates.io crates.io index.crates.io
# [java]   repo.maven.apache.org
